cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, its corpus, or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "ReviewLens: an LLM Java code reviewer, and a human check on the judges that score it"
abstract: >-
  ReviewLens is an LLM-based Java pull request reviewer and an empirical study
  of its own evaluation. It reviews merged pull requests from JUnit 5, Mockito
  and Checkstyle at their pre-review state and measures recall against the
  review comments real maintainers left on them (328 comments across 90 PRs).
  Recall for the one model run over the full corpus is 1.6% (5 of 318 human
  comments on the 87 PRs it covered); all five of those matches were verified
  by a human. Two frozen LLM judges score the pipeline and both were checked
  against a human rater: the matcher held, with 12 of 13 verdicts upheld across
  two censuses, while the hallucination screen agreed at chance level (Cohen's
  kappa = 0.046) and its per-arm result is retracted. That contrast — a frozen,
  deterministic, rubric-driven judge is not thereby a correct one — is the
  study's primary finding.
type: software
authors:
